      "file": "scenes/scene-1.js",
      "narration": "Short sentences add weight. Longer ones carry the listener along. And give each sentence just one idea, so nobody has to hold two at once.",
      "storyboard": "This scene sits on a paper stage, and the visual metaphor is a big amber dial at the left. On 'Short sentences' the dial snaps left and a chunky block of text thuds down with weight. On 'carry the listener along' the dial turns right and a long ribbon of text glides across the frame like a conveyor. On 'one idea' the ribbon collapses into a single 120px word, 'One idea.', on the right. The bullet list is cut.",
      "minDuration": 10,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Use sentence length as a dial",
        "text": "Short sentences slow things down. Longer sentences carry the listener along. One idea per sentence",
        "notes": "Short sentences add weight. Longer ones carry the listener along. And give each sentence just one idea, so nobody has to hold two at once.",
