      "file": "scenes/scene-2.js",
      "narration": "Full stops and questions create pauses. Use them to set up what you want remembered. So how many finished the study? Just over half.",
      "storyboard": "We return to a night stage with a teal waveform running across the frame. On 'Full stops' a giant coral period drops onto the line and the wave goes flat. On 'questions' a huge question mark rises and the wave lifts in pitch. On 'finished the study?' everything holds in complete stillness for a beat. Then 'Just over half.' lands at 150px in amber, with the pause sitting visibly before the answer. The punctuation bullets are rebuilt as these glyphs.",
      "minDuration": 11,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Punctuation is your pause control",
        "text": "Full stop: a clear pause. Comma: a short breath. Question mark: tone change and pause. Pause before the number, not after",
        "notes": "Full stops and questions create pauses. Use them to set up what you want remembered. So how many finished the study? Just over half.",
        "image": "assets/slide-3.png"
      },
